=== Trust-Region Methods for Saddle-Point Problems

With Qiang Du at Columbia University, I am developing trust-region saddle-point algorithms with global convergence as a central goal. The local analysis uses local convexity–concavity assumptions, while our current route to global convergence requires globally strong convexity–concavity. A key objective is to weaken these restrictive global curvature assumptions and address more general saddle-point problems.

=== Applications in Quantum Computing, Biomedical Science, and Scientific Engineering

- [https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.25730.24003 A Two-Stage Variational Quantum Solver for Random-Feature PDE Discretizations] — preprint, 2026.

I am exploring AI-assisted optimization for biological and biomedical problems, including learning stochastic differential equations for biological networks and studying combined virotherapy–chemotherapy models. These projects emphasize model validation, uncertainty, and numerical evidence.
- [https://doi.org/10.23919/ACC.2019.8814709 Parametric Resonant Control of Macroscopic Behaviors of Multiple Oscillators] — /American Control Conference/, 2019.
- [https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCC54389.2021.9674410 Simulation of Folded-Waveguide Space Traveling-Wave Tubes with Derivative-Free Mixed-Integer NEWUOA] — /ICCC/, 2021.
- [https://doi.org/10.11648/j.acm.20241305.13 The Modeling and Optimization of a Multi-Dam System] — /Applied and Computational Mathematics/, 2024.
